  ('Write the oxidation half-equation for Mg forming Mg²⁺.', 'Mg → Mg²⁺ + 2e⁻. Magnesium loses two electrons, so it is oxidised. Charge is balanced: 0 on the left and +2 − 2 = 0 on the right.'),
